#: .\documentation\templates\documentation\docs\customization.html:84
msgid "1. Configuration via settings.py"
msgstr "1. Konfiguration über settings.py"

#: .\documentation\templates\documentation\docs\customization.html:86
#, python-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"                    The %(settings)s dictionary in your Django settings controls app-level options like branding assets, SEO metadata, and feature flags.\n"
"                "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"Das %(settings)s-Dictionary in den Django-Einstellungen steuert Optionen auf App-Ebene wie Branding-Elemente, SEO-Metadaten und Feature-Flags."

#: .\documentation\templates\documentation\docs\customization.html:130
msgid "Loading the Config in Views"
msgstr "Laden der Konfiguration in Views"

#: .\documentation\templates\documentation\docs\customization.html:132
msgid ""
"\n"
"                        To make the configuration available in your templates, import <code class=\"inline-tag\">get_config</code> from <code class=\"inline-tag\">insight_ui.config</code> and add it to your view context.\n"
"                    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"Um die Konfiguration in den Templates verfügbar zu machen, importiere <code class=\"inline-tag\">get_config</code> aus <code class=\"inline-tag\">insight_ui.config</code> und füge es diese View-Kontext hinzu."

#: .\documentation\templates\documentation\docs\customization.html:151
msgid ""
"\n"
"                        The <code class=\"inline-tag\">get_config()</code> function merges your <code class=\"inline-tag\">settings.INSIGHT_UI</code> with the library defaults and returns a dictionary with the key <code class=\"inline-tag\">INSIGHT_UI</code>.\n"
"                    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"Die Funktion <code class=\"inline-tag\">get_config()</code> führt deine <code class=\"inline-tag\">settings.INSIGHT_UI</code> mit den Standardwerten der Bibliothek zusammen und gibt ein Dictionary mit dem Schlüssel <code class=\"inline-tag\">INSIGHT_UI</code> zurück."

#: .\documentation\templates\documentation\docs\customization.html:154
msgid ""
"\n"
"                        Templates can then access the configuration via <code class=\"inline-tag\">&#123;&#123; INSIGHT_UI.title &#125;&#125;</code>, etc.\n"
"                    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"Die Templates können dann über <code class=\"inline-tag\">&#123;&#123; INSIGHT_UI.title &#125;&#125;</code> usw. auf die Konfiguration zugreifen."

#: .\documentation\templates\documentation\docs\customization.html:165
msgid "2. Design Tokens (input.css)"
msgstr "2. Design-Tokens (input.css)"

#: .\documentation\templates\documentation\docs\customization.html:167
#, python-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"                    The %(input)s file is the single source of truth for your visual design. All tokens are defined in the %(theme)s block and automatically apply to all components.\n"
"                "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"Die Datei %(input)s ist die einzige verlässliche Quelle für das visuelles Design. Alle Tokens werden im Block %(theme)s definiert und gelten automatisch für alle Komponenten."

#: .\documentation\templates\documentation\docs\customization.html:174
msgid "Setup: Tailwind CLI"
msgstr "Einrichtung: Tailwind-CLI"

#: .\documentation\templates\documentation\docs\customization.html:176
msgid ""
"\n"
"                        To customize the theme, you need the Tailwind compiler. We recommend <b>django-tailwind-cli</b>.\n"
"                    "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"Um das Theme anzupassen, wird der Tailwind-Compiler benötigt. Wir empfehlen <b>django-tailwind-cli</b>."

#: .\documentation\templates\documentation\docs\customization.html:185
